/*********************************************************************
Configuration and initialization file of the MySQL <Project> database.
MySQL has no schemas inside a database (SCHEMA is a synonym of
DATABASE), so the objects of the application live in one database and
are grouped by directory rather than by schema; create a separate
database only for a part of the application that is deployed on its
own.

All the DDL statements are guarded, i.e., the initialization scripts
should not fail if an object exists: tables use IF NOT EXISTS, views
use OR REPLACE, and routines and triggers are dropped (IF EXISTS) and
created again. MySQL commits every DDL statement implicitly, so the
run cannot be rolled back as one transaction; a failure leaves the
earlier statements in place, and a second run completes the rest.

The script runs with the mysql client from this directory, which
stops at the first error in batch mode (never pass --force):

    mysql -u <owner-user> -p < initialize.sql

Plugins and components are server-level: install them once per
server from ``plugins/`` and ``components/``, never from this file.

The database, its tables and the session use utf8mb4, since utf8
(utf8mb3) cannot store four-byte characters. The rules target MySQL
8.0.19 and later, including the 8.4 LTS release.

Copyright © [<year>] <copyright-holder>
*********************************************************************/

SELECT CONCAT(
    'Starting <Project> Initialization '
    , DATE_FORMAT(NOW(3), '%Y-%m-%d %H:%i:%s.%f')
) AS message;

SET NAMES utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci;

CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS <database>
    CHARACTER SET utf8mb4
    COLLATE utf8mb4_0900_ai_ci;

USE <database>;

/*********************************************************************
Objects of the database are loaded in a strict order from their own
directories under ``schemas/<database>/``: types and lookups, then
tables, functions, procedures, views and triggers, the dated
migrations, and the seeds last. The order ensures all the constraints
are valid and the migrations run before any data is inserted.
*********************************************************************/

SELECT '  >> Creating Database Object(s) (optionally seed) ...'
    AS message;

SOURCE schemas/<database>/initialize.sql

SELECT 'Completed <Project> Initialization' AS message;
